WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.732
A standard view stores a query definition.

00:00:02.732 --> 00:00:08.492
It does not normally store a separate snapshot of the result.

00:00:08.492 --> 00:00:14.727
When the view is queried, PostgreSQL uses the view definition to access current underlying data.

00:00:14.727 --> 00:00:18.587
For consumers, the view behaves like a named relation with columns and rows.

00:00:18.587 --> 00:00:24.237
A standard view stores a query definition, not a separate copy of the rows.

00:00:24.237 --> 00:00:31.667
Treat the selected columns, names, types, and grain as a contract with downstream users.

00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:38.320
Changing that contract can break dashboards or applications even if the underlying query still runs.
